{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/tabs.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:44.761293Z","id":"2bc848571f23757fa0e3645af33dba908af5cb1adc55aa089168ee5554dcb4f7","body":{"detail":"`tooLong` (web/extension/src/sw/tabs.ts:479-489) keeps the tab on (`on` unchanged) but sets its record's `url` to \"\". `persist` (line 235) writes only records with a truthy `url`, and `saved` (lines 97-101) would reject an empty one on restore anyway. After Chrome restarts the service worker, `restore` has no record for that tab, so `tabs.onOrigin(tabId)` is null; the overlay's next message (its 20 s `ping`, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts:394) fails `admitted` in web/extension/src/sw/background.ts:191-198 and is answered `REFUSED`, which stops the overlay (overlay-app.ts:127). The tab's side-panel options outlive the worker, so the panel stays open showing `enabled: false`, and nothing tells the person why Clax went off, unlike the other ways it turns off (background.ts:182 sets a title). The same tab with a short URL survives a restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":229},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"6306d7ef56cae670957bf93882fe53c6a83489be4f94be6ecbac293c55da48ba"},"suggested_fix":"Persist the on/active/overlay/commentMode essentials independently of the URL: keep the record with `url: \"\"` (or a `tooLong: true` flag) and let `saved` accept it when `on` is set, so a restarted worker still admits the overlay and shows the url_too_long notice. Add a tabs.test.ts case: a too-long route, then a fresh `Tabs` over the same store keeps `onOrigin`.","summary":"A tab Clax is on whose URL is over MAX_URL is not persisted, so a worker restart silently turns Clax off in it","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/picks.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:44.761400Z","id":"22c4e99543b31d611a0831a5a93a3695999f9d922ffc166beaa5eb181f3be2b7","body":{"detail":"`Picks.capture` awaits `tabActive(tabId)` (a `chrome.tabs.get`) and only then calls `capture(windowId, …)`, which is `chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab(windowId)` (web/extension/src/sw/capture.ts:25): it captures whatever tab is active in that window when Chrome runs it. If the person switches tabs between the two calls, and Clax holds activeTab or the host permission for the newly active tab (any other tab Clax is on, or any origin granted through `origins.ask`), the clip of that other page, possibly of another origin, is attached to this page's thread and posted to the daemon (picks.ts:277), where agents read it. The window is short (two IPC round trips after a click), so this is unlikely, but the check as written does not guarantee what its comment at picks.ts:131-132 says.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"6ec271e7456934d1bc502e3ad152eb2c734aaefc64599e48b2bd97e8cf4e20d7"},"suggested_fix":"After `capture` resolves, check `tabActive(tabId)` again (and that the tab is still in `windowId`); if it is no longer active, drop the PNG and answer `capture_failed`. A picks.test.ts case can flip `tabActive` from true to false during the fake capture.","summary":"The pick's screenshot can be of another tab: the tab is checked active before `captureVisibleTab`, not after","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/tabs.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:16.140201Z","id":"e1ec635224227de3daf796bd59e86d297aa3921e9cdc37146a9e706890294ad9","body":{"detail":"web/extension/src/sw/tabs.ts:479-489 spreads the old state (keeping `on`) with `url: \"\"`; line 235 persists only `if (s.url)`; `saved` (lines 97-101) also requires /^https?:\\/\\// on url. After restore, onOrigin (line 180) is null, so `admitted` (web/extension/src/sw/background.ts:191-198) fails and line 212 returns REFUSED, which stops the overlay (web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts:126 `if (isRefusal(r)) { stop(); ...}`), triggered by the PING_MS ping at overlay-app.ts:394. No title or notice is set on this path, unlike background.ts:182. Kind concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"2bc848571f23757fa0e3645af33dba908af5cb1adc55aa089168ee5554dcb4f7","summary":"confirmed: tooLong keeps `on` but blanks `url`, persist skips url-less records, so a restarted worker refuses the tab's overlay","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/picks.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:16.140353Z","id":"3fd891357c7cc3ee46a01fb5066d8ba47ffb152db9c8e45d39123cfd747e7b6b","body":{"detail":"web/extension/src/sw/picks.ts:143-144 awaits tabActive then `this.d.capture(windowId, ...)`; web/extension/src/sw/background.ts wires capture to captureClip(chromeCapture, windowId, ...) and web/extension/src/sw/capture.ts:25 is `chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab(windowId, ...)`, which captures the window's active tab at call time. Nothing re-checks after the capture resolves (line 145 checks only the pick identity). The doc comment at picks.ts:130-133 says nothing is captured when the tab is no longer active. Low-probability race; kind suggestion fits.","kind":"comment","references":"22c4e99543b31d611a0831a5a93a3695999f9d922ffc166beaa5eb181f3be2b7","summary":"confirmed: tabActive is checked before captureVisibleTab and not after, so a tab switch in between captures another tab","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/picks.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:32:15.800742Z","id":"b823f74615d0986cc733b663baec21f4fec7e812c6a180e78dda589077d88396","body":{"detail":"Picks.capture checks that the pick's tab is its window's active tab before and after `capture` (`chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab(windowId)`, web/extension/src/sw/capture.ts), which captures whatever tab is active when Chrome takes it. If the person switches to another tab B and back to the pick's tab A while the capture runs, both checks see A active, but the PNG can be of B: possibly another origin whose page Clax holds activeTab or a host grant for. It is then attached to A's thread and posted to the daemon, where agents read it. The window is a few IPC round trips, so it needs two switches inside it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"013d51ffe662bf31ef9e25a831ebb6cff0d25a08b959b761f73126aaefda0920"},"suggested_fix":"Count `chrome.tabs.onActivated` events per window in the worker (web/extension/src/sw/background.ts already listens to it, line 147), pass the count to Picks, read it before the capture and after, and drop the shot as capture_failed when it changed. A picks.test.ts case can bump the count during the fake capture.","summary":"A quick A->B->A tab switch during a pick's capture passes both active checks and attaches tab B's screenshot","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/picks.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:04:32.674523Z","id":"439f1ea1ad820a0ff30e77c40164b49638a83c721d6d769c7876b3cd45196cd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1e4a6480b","summary":"Fixed: tabActive(tabId, windowId) is checked before and after captureVisibleTab, with the tab's window; picks.test.ts \"drops a screenshot taken after the pick's tab stopped being the window's active tab\" and \"captures nothing when the pick's tab is in another window\" pass (failed before). The A-B-A switch is concern b823f746.","supersedes":"22c4e99543b31d611a0831a5a93a3695999f9d922ffc166beaa5eb181f3be2b7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/sw/tabs.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:04:32.732263Z","id":"a1e6447129de12e77c6bffa39d7616a0e2f9092863bc1e30c552ff5d176f0782","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b099e0db5","summary":"Fixed: a tab with Clax on is kept across worker restarts with an empty URL when its address is over MAX_URL; tabs.test.ts \"keeps Clax on through a worker restart in a tab whose address is over MAX_URL\" passes (failed before).","supersedes":"2bc848571f23757fa0e3645af33dba908af5cb1adc55aa089168ee5554dcb4f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
